                                       ├─ ServiceNow CR & CTASK Generation
                                       └─ CSV Audit Logging (db2_drift_audit.csv)
Key FeaturesDirect Raw Parameter Analysis: Connects to DB2 instances via native ibm_db drivers to query sysibmadm.dbcfg and sysibmadm.dbmcfg parameters without requiring pre-computed diff logic.Smart AUTOMATIC Parity Handling: Recognizes when parameters on Primary and Standby evaluate to DB2's AUTOMATIC tuning flag and avoids false positive drift alerts.DBA Mentoring Mode: Uses Azure AI Foundry (LLM) to translate parameter mismatches into clear business and technical risk explanations without jargon.Spotlight Top 3 Differences: Highlights the top three parameter mismatches categorized by Performance, Recovery Time, or Failover Reliability.Automated ServiceNow Change Request (CR) & CTASK Generation: Automatically constructs a complete ServiceNow Change Request template (Short Description, Description, Impact, Implementation Plan, Backout Plan, Testing Plan) alongside distinct CTASKs for the Application and DBA teams.Dynamic Outage Classification: Classifies changes as IMMEDIATE (dynamic update, no downtime required) or DEFERRED (requires database/application restart) and updates the ServiceNow outage fields automatically.Persistent CSV Audit Log: Appends every scan result, risk rating, timestamp, and target node list to a local db2_drift_audit.csv file with a one-click CSV export option in the UI.Project StructurePlaintextdb2-drift-poc/
