Setup & Deployment GuidePhase 1: Azure Infrastructure & Azure AI Foundry SetupStep 1: Create Resource GroupLog in to the Azure Portal.Search for Resource groups in the top search bar and click + Create.Select your Subscription.Resource Group Name: rg-db2-hadrRegion: East US (or your preferred region)Click Review + Create > Create.Step 2: Create Virtual Network (VNet) and SubnetSearch for Virtual networks in the top search bar and click + Create.Basics Tab:Resource Group: rg-db2-hadrName: vnet-db2Region: East USIP Addresses Tab:IPv4 Address space: 10.10.0.0/16Click + Add subnet:Subnet name: db2-subnetSubnet address range: 10.10.1.0/24Click Review + create > Create.Step 3: Configure Network Security Group (NSG)Search for Network security groups and click + Create.Name: nsg-db2-driftResource Group: rg-db2-hadrRegion: East USOnce created, open nsg-db2-drift and go to Inbound security rules > + Add:Rule 1 (SSH): Port 22, Priority 100, Name Allow-SSHRule 2 (HTTP App Console): Port 80, Priority 110, Name Allow-HTTPRule 3 (DB2 Listener): Port 50000, Priority 120, Name Allow-DB2-EngineRule 4 (HADR Sync Port): Port 60000, Priority 130, Name Allow-HADR-SyncAssociate this NSG with db2-subnet under Subnets > + Associate.Step 4: Azure AI Foundry SetupSearch for Azure AI Foundry (or Azure OpenAI).Create a new resource named foundry-db2-drift in rg-db2-hadr.Under Model Deployments, deploy a base model (e.g., DeepSeek-V3 or GPT-4) and set the Deployment Name to: db2-drift-analyzerGo to Keys and Endpoint and copy your Endpoint URL, Deployment Name, and API Key.Phase 2: App Server VM Setup & DeploymentSSH into vm-db2-drift-app (10.10.1.100):Bashssh azureuser@10.10.1.100
