Phase 3: DB2 Node VM & IBM DB2 11.5 HADR Setup GuideStep 1: Provision DB2 Virtual Machines on AzureDeploy DB2 nodes in vnet-db2 (db2-subnet):Server HostnameRolePrivate IPOSSizeprimary-appa-01App A Primary10.10.1.4RHEL 9.xStandard_D4s_v5secondary-appa-02App A Standby10.10.1.5RHEL 9.xStandard_D4s_v5primary-appb-01App B Primary10.10.2.4RHEL 9.xStandard_D4s_v5secondary-appb-02App B Standby10.10.2.5RHEL 9.xStandard_D4s_v5Step 2: Prerequisites & OS ConfigurationExecute these commands on ALL DB2 nodes:Bash# Update OS & install DB2 dependencies
sudo dnf update -y
sudo dnf install -y libaio glibc.i686 libstdc++ ksh pam.i686 numactl file

# Configure kernel tuning parameters for DB2
cat << 'EOF' | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/99-db2.conf
kernel.shmmax = 18446744073709551615
kernel.msgmni = 1024
fs.file-max = 65536
EOF

sudo sysctl --system

# Update security limits
cat << 'EOF' | sudo tee -a /etc/security/limits.conf
db2inst1 soft data -1
db2inst1 hard data -1
db2inst1 soft fsize -1
db2inst1 hard fsize -1
db2inst1 soft nofile 65536
db2inst1 hard nofile 65536
EOF

# Create DB2 Groups and Users
sudo groupadd -g 1001 db2iadm1
sudo groupadd -g 1002 db2fadm1
sudo useradd -u 1001 -g db2iadm1 -m -d /home/db2inst1 db2inst1
sudo useradd -u 1002 -g db2fadm1 -m -d /home/db2fenc1 db2fenc1
echo "db2inst1" | sudo passwd --stdin db2inst1
Step 3: Install IBM DB2 11.5 EngineExecute on ALL DB2 nodes:Bash# Upload/extract your IBM DB2 v11.5 installer tarball
tar -xvzf v11.5_linuxx64_dec.tar.gz
cd v11.5_linuxx64_dec

# Run silent installation
sudo ./db2_install -b /opt/ibm/db2/v11.5 -p SERVER -n

# Create DB2 Instance
sudo /opt/ibm/db2/v11.5/instance/db2icrt -u db2fenc1 db2inst1

# Configure Instance Communications
sudo su - db2inst1 -c "db2 update dbm cfg using svcename 50000"
sudo su - db2inst1 -c "db2set DB2COMM=TCPIP"
sudo su - db2inst1 -c "db2start"
Phase 4: Application A HADR Cluster SetupStep 1: Configure Primary (primary-appa-01 - 10.10.1.4)Bashsudo su - db2inst1

# Create Database and enable Archival Logging
db2 "CREATE DATABASE KYDB2A AUTOMATIC STORAGE YES"
mkdir -p /home/db2inst1/archlogs /home/db2inst1/backups
db2 "UPDATE DB CFG FOR KYDB2A USING LOGARCHMETH1 DISK:/home/db2inst1/archlogs"

# Configure HADR parameters on Primary
db2 "UPDATE DB CFG FOR KYDB2A USING HADR_LOCAL_HOST 10.10.1.4"
db2 "UPDATE DB CFG FOR KYDB2A USING HADR_LOCAL_SVC 60000"
db2 "UPDATE DB CFG FOR KYDB2A USING HADR_REMOTE_HOST 10.10.1.5"
db2 "UPDATE DB CFG FOR KYDB2A USING HADR_REMOTE_SVC 60000"
db2 "UPDATE DB CFG FOR KYDB2A USING HADR_REMOTE_INST db2inst1"
db2 "UPDATE DB CFG FOR KYDB2A USING HADR_SYNCMODE NEARSYNC"
db2 "UPDATE DB CFG FOR KYDB2A USING HADR_TIMEOUT 120"

